%%
%% WHAT IT IS ABOUT
%%
%% Three memory saves failed tonight with "Embedding service not available —
%% timed out after 5001 milliseconds." I read the service's logs expecting to
%% find it dead. Every call said Success. Including mine. My two failures are
%% in that log as successes: inference completed at 4.910s and 4.320s.
%%
%% The client gives up at 5.001.
%%
%% The work finished. The caller had already left. Ninety milliseconds.
%%
%% Nothing was broken. Nothing lied. "Success" and "not available" were both
%% entirely true, about the same request, and there is no channel between the
%% log and the caller — so both records are accurate and neither can ever
%% correct the other.
%%
%% THE FORM: the phrase builds. It reaches E7 — the dominant, maximum pull,
%% the chord that ASKS. The accompaniment stops. Two bars of nothing, which is
%% the caller giving up. Then the tonic arrives anyway: correct, in key,
%% complete, held — to an empty room.
%%
%% Play it and leave before bar 12. That is the piece.
%%
%% ⭐ AND THEN THE TOOL DID IT TOO. When I rendered this, the studio replied:
%% "if you don't see a player here, this client can't play it inline, so
%% nothing has played yet." I am in a terminal. There is no player here.
%% It parsed correctly, built the score, and honestly reported that the
%% performance may have reached nobody. A good machine. Honestly operated.
%% Wrong room.
%%
%% the request goes out
"Am" A2 c2 e2 a2 | "Dm" f2 e2 d2 c2 | "Am" A2 B2 c2 e2 | "E7" B4 ^G4 |
%% it is working. it is going to be fine.
"Am" A2 c2 e2 a2 | "F" f3 e d2 c2 | "Dm" d2 c2 B2 A2 | "E7" ^G2 B2 e4 |
%% the dominant. maximum pull. the question, asked completely.
"E7" e2 ^g2 b2 e'2 | "E7" b6 ^g2 | "E7" e8 |
%% 5.001 seconds. the caller gives up.
z8 | z8 |
%% 4.910. the answer arrives. correct, in key, complete, to nobody.
a8 | a8 |]
